-- More idioms of the day. Not a migration: paste this into the Supabase SQL editor and run it.
-- Safe to re-run (existing `spanish` values are skipped). Appending keeps the order of the
-- rotation (it is ordered by `seq`), though which idiom lands on a given day shifts as the list
-- grows.
--
-- Selection: Spanish proverbs, set phrases and multi-word verb idioms from English Wiktionary
-- (Category:Spanish idioms and Category:Spanish proverbs), excluding entries labelled vulgar,
-- offensive, derogatory, obsolete, archaic, dated or rare, plus a manual pass for crude or bland
-- ones. Only idioms with a real example sentence are included. Meanings follow each entry's
-- first sense and are CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://en.wiktionary.org), linked per row in `source_url`.
-- Example sentences come from Tatoeba (https://tatoeba.org, CC BY 2.0 FR), credited per row with
-- the sentence ID and contributor, or are the Wiktionary entry's own usage example where marked.
-- See ATTRIBUTIONS.md. Rows whose `spanish` already exists are skipped.

on conflict (spanish) do nothing;
